<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n87895" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Προκύων</span></b> 
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">[ῠ]</span><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">,
			κῠνός, ὁ,</span> the star <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>Procyon,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Arat.
				450
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hipparch.
				2.2.13
			</span></i>, etc.; but of Sirius, <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				17(1).17
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρόκυνες, οἱ,</span>
			<i>winds which precede the rising of Sirius,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Adam.
				<u>Vent.</u>
				41
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>spaniel-like flatterer, 'lap-dog',</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Phld.
				<u>Rh.</u>
				1.242
			</span></i>
			<i><span class="en">
				S.
			</span></i>, prob. l. for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρόσκυνες</span> in <i><span class="en">
				Hippias Erythr.
			</span></i> I: but <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πικροὶ Καλλιμάχου
			πρόκυνες,</span> a description of the Grammarians, <i>snappers
				and snarlers,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				AP
				11.322
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Antiphan.
			</span></i>).</div>
